/target

# Rust build lockfile — this crate is a library, so we do
# not commit our own Cargo.lock. Anchored so the nested
# `fuzz/Cargo.lock` (a binary harness — `publish = false`) is
# allowed through to pin the libfuzzer / oxideav-core resolution
# against a known bytewise-identical fuzz environment.
# See https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/faq.html#why-do-binaries-have-cargolock-in-version-control-but-not-libraries
/Cargo.lock
